.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trellis-exec 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-exec \- Run an arbitrary command in each package directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis exec\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-serial\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPACKAGES\fR] <\fICOMMAND\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an arbitrary command in each package directory
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<REF>\fR
Only packages owning files changed since this git ref
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to color output. `auto` follows the terminal, `NO_COLOR`, and `CLICOLOR=0`; the other two override that detection
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-serial\fR
Run one package at a time, in dependency order
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR
Keep scheduling packages after a failure
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress normal\-path output; JSON/report payloads and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum concurrent packages (default: CPU count)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Trace every command trellis shells out to, on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the `trellis.exec/1` payload instead of the summary table; package output moves to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Don\*(Aqt check whether a newer trellis release is available

The check is also skipped in CI, when not attached to a terminal, and when `TRELLIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPACKAGES\fR]
Packages to run in; all workspace packages when omitted
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
The command to run (after `\-\-`)
